 # OpenDAoC
 [![Build and Release](https://github.com/OpenDAoC/OpenDAoC-Core/actions/workflows/build-and-release.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/OpenDAoC/OpenDAoC-Core/actions/workflows/build-and-release.yml)
 
-> **Modified version.** This branch is a fork of [OpenDAoC/OpenDAoC-Core](https://github.com/OpenDAoC/OpenDAoC-Core) at commit f0aaa1ea2 (tag 2026.09.36), used by [daoc-sdk](https://github.com/gartmeier/daoc-sdk). Joshua Gartmeier changed `GameServer/gameutils/GamePlayerUtils.cs` on 2026-11-10: `UpdateUsableSkills` replaces a cached skill whenever the player holds a different instance of it, so after `/player class` the skill list shows the current specialization levels, where before it kept the old ones until a relog. Everything else, including the rest of this README, is upstream's. Report problems with this change at daoc-sdk, and anything else upstream.
+> **Modified version.** This branch is a fork of [OpenDAoC/OpenDAoC-Core](https://github.com/OpenDAoC/OpenDAoC-Core) at commit f0aaa1ea2 (tag 2026.09.36), used by [daoc-sdk](https://github.com/gartmeier/daoc-sdk). Joshua Gartmeier changed two files. `GameServer/gameutils/GamePlayerUtils.cs` on 2026-11-10: `UpdateUsableSkills` replaces a cached skill whenever the player holds a different instance of it, so after `/player class` the skill list shows the current specialization levels, where before it kept the old ones until a relog. `GameServer/gameobjects/GamePlayer.cs` on 2026-11-11: a trade opens under both players' trade locks, so two players adding an item or money to each other in the same tick share one window, where before they could each open their own and hang the whole server at their next adds. Everything else, including the rest of this README, is upstream's. Report problems with these changes at daoc-sdk, and anything else upstream.
 
